# agent CLI: hermes — Hermes Agent (https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent) — a
# gateway/api-key agent like opencode/pi/omp. It reaches models ONLY through the platform
# gateway: an `aip-gateway` provider (base_url → the host nginx gateway :18787, which
# forwards to LiteLLM) is written KEYLESS to the GLOBAL ~/.hermes/config.yaml at workspace
# start (the provider's key_env NAMES the AIP_GATEWAY_KEY env var, resolved at runtime —
# never a real provider secret; LiteLLM holds the real credentials, arch §17). Headroom
# input-compression applies automatically at the gateway (LiteLLM pre_call guardrail).
# The installer bundles its own uv/Python/Node; the OS base already ships python/uv/node.
# NOTE: hermes is NOT installed at image build. Its uv venv is path-sensitive, and ~/.hermes
# is symlink-migrated to the /persist overlay at workspace start; a build-baked venv lost its
# pyvenv.cfg + deps across that migration and `hermes` failed with ModuleNotFoundError. It is
# instead installed at workspace START by workspace.Manager.registerHermes (detached,
# once-guarded, best-effort), which builds a complete venv at the final ~/.hermes path.
# This snippet is intentionally a no-op marker so the build stays cache-stable for hermes.
USER workspace
